9. why prefer method level and in the service method only
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Why Use Method-Level Security?

Imagine later you have two endpoints calling the same service method:

DELETE /accounts/10

and:

POST /admin/accounts/delete/10

Both eventually call:

deleteAccount(id);

If you secure only one URL:

DELETE /accounts/**

the other endpoint might need another security rule.

But if the actual service method is protected:

@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
public void deleteAccount(Long id)

then:

Any caller
    ↓
deleteAccount()
    ↓
ADMIN required

So the important business operation itself is protected.


we can use hasanyrole, has authority same like in the url based





